  "rule": "One 9x9 D4-symmetric frame of 3x3 tiles with an empty centre tile sits on background 8. Each of the eight outer tiles is mirrored across its outer edge and stamped one tile further out: edge tiles are flipped once and corners rotated 180 degrees, giving a 15x15 star that is clipped at the canvas border. The 3x3 hole is filled from the surrounding 5x5 ring. Centre (i,j) takes ring (2i,2j), and the middle cell takes ring (0,1).",
  "scope": "Supported: a single D4-symmetric frame built from a transpose-symmetric corner tile and an LR-symmetric edge tile. The palette has 2-4 colours, or more when supplied tiles bring more. Canvases are 15..30 by default and 9..30 when explicit, and may be non-square. Placement is random, and about 12% of draws (or clip=True) clip the star. Explicit width, height, row, col, corner, edge and clip are all honoured or rejected with ValueError. Synthetic extensions: sides above 19, non-square canvases and clipped stars, none of which appear in the fixtures. Not supported: asymmetric frames, multiple frames, backgrounds other than 8, frames other than 9x9.",
  "constraints": [
    "Reviewed D4-symmetric latent tile construction, outward stamping, centre fill, clipping and colour plurality checks",
