  "authored_scope": "Supported: a single D4-symmetric frame built from a transpose-symmetric corner tile and an LR-symmetric edge tile. The palette has 2-4 colours, or more when supplied tiles bring more. Canvases are 15..30 by default and 9..30 when explicit, and may be non-square. Placement is random, and about 12% of draws (or clip=True) clip the star. Explicit width, height, row, col, corner, edge and clip are all honoured or rejected with ValueError. Synthetic extensions: sides above 19, non-square canvases and clipped stars, none of which appear in the fixtures. Not supported: asymmetric frames, multiple frames, backgrounds other than 8, frames other than 9x9.",
  "authored_constraints": [
    "Colour 8 is the strict plurality colour of the input, so background detection is unambiguous.",
    "Frame tiles never contain colour 8, so the non-background bounding box is exactly the 9x9 frame and the hole is exactly the central 3x3.",
    "The frame lies fully inside the canvas; only the outward copies may be clipped.",
    "Sampled tiles: the three centre sources (corner[2][2], edge[2][0], edge[2][1]) are never all equal, and are pairwise distinct in about 60% of draws when achievable.",
    "Sampled tiles usually have non-trivial mirroring: edge row0 != row2, and corner rot180 differs from identity and from a single flip.",
    "Explicit clip must be consistent with explicit offsets and sides, otherwise ValueError."
  ],
  "semantic_review": {
    "status": "reviewed",
    "checks": [
      "Reviewed D4-symmetric latent tile construction, outward stamping, centre fill, clipping and colour plurality checks",
      "Middle-cell selection is underdetermined by canonical examples; decorrelation samples are explicitly recorded as an inferred rule extension",
      "1000 independent seeds 20000..20999 pass; native uniqueness count 1000",
      "100 additional seeds 61000..61099 pass; all change output; 30 successful parameter controls and 6 expected invalid rejections",
      "Original canonical fixture replay exact; no query-specific output lookup used",
      "1000 independent seeds 20000..20999; approved validation fixtures reconstructed exactly; canonical replay reported separately"
    ],
    "limitations": [
      "When both tiles are supplied, no non-degeneracy repairs run; monochrome tiles are accepted (needed for fixture-style tiles).",
      "The modal-colour decorrelation is a bounded best-effort search. Its achieved rate is below the ~50% attempt rate and has not been measured.",
      "The middle-cell semantics (ring (0,1)) cannot be fully separated by the fixtures from alternatives such as the modal colour or the edge tile's side cell. The generator decorrelates them in a fraction of draws but does not guarantee it.",
      "Clipped stars and large or non-square canvases are synthetic extensions not present in the fixtures.",
      "Bounded solver agreement and control checks do not prove complete coverage of every interpretation of the task."
    ]
